sentences.l:
and not then Circe
from Hades having come did we escape the notice of, but very quickly
she came, her preparations made;

But drive past, and over the ears smear of your companions
honey-sweet wax, having kneaded it, lest any hear
of the others;

By that way not even winged things pass, nor the doves,
timorous ones, which ambrosia to father Zeus carry,
but even of these always the smooth rock takes one away;

And the two crags, the one reaches the broad heaven
with sharp peak, and a cloud around it has come to stand
dark;

and there she fishes, around the crag feeling about,
for dolphins and dogs, and if anywhere something bigger she catches,
a sea-beast, which, countless, loud-groaning Amphitrite feeds.
